n\n1. **`^`** - Start of line (with MULTILINE flag)\n\n2. **`(?=.*\\b IPv4_PATTERN \\b)`** - Lookahead that verifies an IPv4 address exists somewhere on the line\n   - IPv4 octet pattern: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])`\n   - Matches 0-255 without leading zeros (e.g., \"001\" or \"010\" won't match)\n   - Four octets separated by dots with word boundaries\n\n3. **`.*`** - Greedy match to consume as much text as possible\n\n4. **`\\b([0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]))\\b`** - Captures the date\n   - Year: 4 digits (any 0000-9999)\n   - Month: 01-12\n   - Day: 01-29 (allows up to 29 for all months per requirements)\n   - Word boundaries ensure dates aren't part of larger alphanumeric sequences\n\n5. **`$`** - End of line\n\n**How it finds the last date:**\nThe greedy `.*` combined with the date pattern and end-of-line anchor causes the regex engine to backtrack and match only the rightmost date on lines containing IPv4 addresses.\n\n**Examples:**\n- `192.168.1.1 logged at 2024-01-15` → matches `2024-01-15` ✓\n- `192.168.1.1 events 2024-01-15 and 2024-01-20` → matches `2024-01-20` (last one) ✓\n- `user1134-12-1234 with 192.168.1.1` → no match (1134-12-1234 isn't valid, and word boundaries protect it) ✓\n- `2024-01-15` without IPv4 → no match ✓","ttft_ms":93832,"type":"result","duration_ms":99581,"uuid":"a129996b-1501-4c93-bc03-0f3e7a8406e3","ttft_stream_ms":829,"time_to_request_ms":79,"queued_turn_count":0}
